{
  "name": "perf-measure",
  "mode": "tool",
  "description": "The compile-throughput measurement library Tools/perf/throughput/measure.mjs (with parseCounters, which it re-exports from Tools/perf/scaling/harness.mjs) and its Jet twin, the Measure module of the jet_perf_kit package (Tools/perf/kit/Source/Measure.jet), #5072 c7, each run by a driver that prints one export's result: readTrace of a live stream (a partial last row, a padded row, rows that are not JSON) and of a closed array; every completed-trace refusal (identity, stream, row, JSON, process identity, schema, window, time order, span category and balance) and the accepted trace; phaseTable (phase spans by name == cat, threads keyed by their text so 1 and \"1\" share spans, unions across threads, items summed the JavaScript way, integer-like kinds first in the JSON object, unclosed kinds, a NaN offset) over sampled CPU; cpuAt before, between, on equal and after samples; parseCounters (both line forms, CRLF, nested counters, an empty phase, a counter summed over lines) and its refusals; sampleTree of a live process tree; runMeasured of `true` under the GNU time it finds on PATH; runMeasured past a 300 ms timeout, which kills the whole measured tree (a background writer never writes); and the constants SAMPLE_MS and GNU_TIME (the sampling interval and the GNU time path, which must exist). The original driver is Tools/gauntlet/harness/drivers/perf-measure.mjs, so the census counts measure.mjs as covered by this entry.",
